   ],
   "role": "small",
   "why": "outside any article",
   "words": 27,
   "text": "patriarch of Islam, Christianity and Judaism. He was the first pioneer of Islam and the original founder-builder of the Kabah. Ahimsa Sanskrit for 'do no harm'; denotes"
  },
  {
   "page": 48,
   "ids": [
    "p48b15"
   ],
   "role": "small",
   "why": "outside any article",
   "words": 28,
   "text": "where the Treaty of Hudaibiya was made between Muhammad representing the state of Medina and the Quraysh tribe of Makkah in 628 AD. Ismael also (Ishmael), firstborn son"
  },
  {
   "page": 48,
   "ids": [
    "p48b3",
    "p48b16"
   ],
   "role": "small",
   "why": "outside any article",
   "words": 58,
   "text": "the principle of non-violence, one of the cardinal virtues of major Indian religions. Aisha (612–678); daughter of Abu Bakr, of Abraham, born to him from his wife Hajira (Hagar). Ismael was also a Prophet and ancestor of Prophet Muhammad, the last prophet of Islam. Jihad struggle in the way of God. Kabah the sacred house of God built"
  },
